sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant API as API Layer
    participant Redis as Redis Cache
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Provider as Stripe/Chapa/Telebirr
    
    Note over C,Provider: SCENARIO 1: First Request (Normal Flow)
    
    C->>+API: POST /payments<br/>Idempotency-Key: order_42
    API->>+Redis: GET idempotency:merchant_id:order_42
    Redis-->>-API: nil (cache miss)
    
    API->>+DB: INSERT payment_intents<br/>WHERE (merchant_id, idempotency_key)<br/>UNIQUE constraint
    DB-->>-API: Success: row inserted
    
    API->>+Provider: CreateCharge(order_42)
    Provider-->>-API: checkout_url, provider_tx_id
    
    API->>+Redis: SET idempotency:merchant_id:order_42<br/>value: {response_body}<br/>TTL: 24h
    Redis-->>-API: OK
    
    API-->>-C: 201 Created<br/>{payment_intent, checkout_url}
    
    Note over C,Provider: SCENARIO 2: Duplicate Request (Idempotency Replay)
    
    C->>+API: POST /payments<br/>Idempotency-Key: order_42<br/>(network retry)
    API->>+Redis: GET idempotency:merchant_id:order_42
    Redis-->>-API: {cached_response}
    
    Note over API: REPLAY cached response<br/>No DB write<br/>No provider call
    
    API-->>-C: 201 Created<br/>{payment_intent, checkout_url}<br/>(identical to first response)
    
    Note over C,Provider: SCENARIO 3: Race Condition (Concurrent Requests)
    
    par Concurrent Request 1
        C->>+API: POST /payments<br/>Idempotency-Key: order_43
        API->>+Redis: GET idempotency:merchant_id:order_43
        Redis-->>-API: nil
        API->>+DB: INSERT payment_intents<br/>UNIQUE(merchant_id, idempotency_key)
        DB-->>-API: Success
        API->>Provider: CreateCharge
        API-->>-C: 201 Created
    and Concurrent Request 2
        C->>+API: POST /payments<br/>Idempotency-Key: order_43<br/>(same key, concurrent)
        API->>+Redis: GET idempotency:merchant_id:order_43
        Redis-->>-API: nil (cache not yet set)
        API->>+DB: INSERT payment_intents<br/>UNIQUE(merchant_id, idempotency_key)
        DB-->>-API: ERROR: duplicate key violation<br/>23505
        Note over API: Detect unique violation<br/>Return 409 Conflict
        API-->>-C: 409 Conflict<br/>idempotency_key already used
    end
    
    Note over C,Provider: Database UNIQUE constraint is the<br/>authoritative source of truth.<br/>Redis cache is performance optimization only.
